    "https://jobs.keldair.com/uindy/Staff/jobs/102110/director-of-housing-and-residence-life": {
      "title": "Director of Housing & Residence Life",
      "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading Director of Housing & Residence Life Indianapolis, IN 46227 Posted: 09/15/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Full-time, Exempt Pay: $65,000.00 - $70,000.00 per Year Department: Student Affairs Experience: Intermediate Apply Job Description At UIndy, we cultivate a vibrant, close-knit residential community on the Southside of Indianapolis. Serving a diverse student body of over 4,200 total students, our department oversees the vibrant home-away-from-home for 1,700 campus residents. We bridge classroom learning with everyday community through six distinctive residence halls housing approximately 900 students, alongside three bustling apartment complexes home to 800 upper-division students. Joining our team means shaping an engaging, inclusive environment where dynamic educational programming, student leadership development, and meaningful relationships empower Greyhounds to thrive. The Director of Housing and Residence Life serves as the senior executive leader for the University’s comprehensive residential enterprise within the Division of Student Affairs and Student Success. Reporting to the Associate Dean of Students, this role provides vision, strategic alignment, and operational leadership across all residential life programs and housing operations for UIndy’s 1,700 on-campus residents across our six residence halls and three apartment communities. The Director directly supervises professional staff members, including the Associate Director for Residence Life and the Coordinator for Housing Operations, fostering a high-performing team dedicated to student engagement, wellbeing, belonging, and success. As the administrative head of the department, the Director bridges business operations with student development, ensuring an integrated residential experience that supports institutional enrollment and student success goals. This is a live-off position, including occasional evening and weekend responsibilities, shared collaboratively with the Housing and Residence Life team. The incumbent of this role serves in the senior-level on-call rotation, providing administrative support and crisis intervention during after-hours emergencies. REQUIREMENTS/MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Personnel, Counseling, Business Administration, or a related field. Experience: Minimum of 5 years post-master’s progressive, full-time professional experience in Residence Life and/or Housing Operations. Supervision: Proven experience directly supervising full-time professional staff. Technical Aptitude: Demonstrated experience managing complex databases or housing software systems. Crisis Management: Experience serving in an on-call capacity and responding to campus emergencies. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Leadership: 3+ years of experience managing multi-tiered supervisory structures or leading departmental operations. Software Expertise: Advanced proficiency in housing management software (e.g., Housing.Cloud), student conduct systems (e.g., Maxient), and occupancy analytics. Strategic Thinking: Demonstrated success in developing retention-focused initiatives, living-learning communities, or streamlining complex operations. Budgetary Oversight: Significant experience managing departmental, operational, and programmatic budgets. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Associate Director of Residence Life Coordinator for Operations ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Strategic Leadership & Organizational Vision Provide strategic direction and administrative vision for Housing and Residence Life, aligning operational systems and residential life initiatives with institutional priorities. Directly supervise, mentor, and evaluate professional staff (Associate Director for Residence Life and Coordinator for Housing Operations), promoting professional growth, clear performance benchmarks, and departmental accountability. Formulate and execute multi-year strategic plans, policy frameworks, and residential living-learning strategies aimed at enhancing student persistence, sense of belonging, and retention. Lead departmental assessment efforts by designing data-informed evaluation metrics regarding occupancy trends, student satisfaction, facility utilization, and learning outcomes. Housing Rate Setting, Fiscal Leadership & Auxiliary Contracting Establish annual housing room-and-board rates, rate tiers, and occupancy financial models in coordination with division and institution leadership. Oversee all apartment leasing and contract processes, in partnership with the Coordinator for Operations, serving as the senior contract manager for university-managed and third-party apartment properties. Develop and implement a marketing plan designed to increase housing occupancy and revenue growth. Direct comprehensive departmental operating budgets, prioritizing strategic allocation of funds for residential programming, facility upgrades, operational technology, and staff development. Serve as the senior university liaison for auxiliary campus partnerships, ensuring high contract performance standards for dining service administration and third-party property management. Champion capital improvement projects, space allocation priorities, and long-term facility master planning in collaboration with Facilities Management. Enterprise System Administration & Operational Infrastructure Serve as the primary System Administrator for all housing and auxiliary software platforms (e.g., Housing.Cloud), ensuring system stability, workflow optimization, user permission control, and data integrity. Partner with Information Technology to direct technical data integrity efforts, system upgrades, custom reporting, and automated data synchronization between the housing enterprise system and the Student Information System (SIS/Banner). Oversee the end-to-end administration of housing contract workflows, room selection engine configurations, fee schedules, damage assessments, and break housing processes. Establish policy standards and governance for campus-wide residential access control systems and key management protocols in partnership with IT and Campus Police. Guide the operational direction of campus facilities within the unit's portfolio, such as the Schwitzer Student Center and the Fitness Hub, ensuring alignment with student needs. Crisis Management, Compliance & Student Support Participate in the senior-level administrative on-call rotation, providing leadership and directive guidance during critical after-hours campus emergencies. Collaborate closely with the Associate Dean of Students, Greyhound Support Team (BIT), and student conduct officers to support residential students of concern and manage high-level behavioral interventions. Ensure departmental compliance with all federal, state, and institutional mandates, including Title IX, FERPA, Clery Act, and VAWA guidelines. Build strong collaborative partnerships across Academic Affairs, Student Affairs & Student Success, University Events, Disability Resources, and Financial Aid to promote a holistic student experience. Company Description Thank you for your interest in the University of Indianapolis! The University is a private, comprehensive teaching university located on 65 acres just minutes from downtown Indianapolis. With more than 700 faculty and staff, it is a place where you can become part of a close-knit campus community that emphasizes the importance of community partnerships in the future growth of the University. UIndy’s mission is to prepare its graduates for effective, responsible, and articulate membership in the complex societies in which they live and serve and for excellence and leadership in their personal and professional lives. The motto of \"Education for Service\" provides the foundation for our work to better our communities, both near and far. As University employees, we know the work we do is important to our students and our communities. To accomplish our mission, we welcome talented, civic-minded, and diverse individuals from all career levels to help maintain our high standards of excellence and quality. If you want to join our dynamic environment and experience hard work, creativity, and teamwork, we welcome your application! The University of Indianapolis is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, disability, citizenship status, military status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. The University of Indianapolis does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment and admission as required by Title IX. Benefits Medical Insurance Vision Insurance Dental Insurance Life Insurance Tuition Discount Retirement Savings Plan - 403B Paid Vacation and Sick Time Accruals Paid Holiday time and additional University days off Employee Discounts & Services Free Parking Onsite Health & Wellness Center For more information about the benefits of being a staff member at UIndy, visit our Benefits site. Apply The University of Indianapolis is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, disability, citizenship status, military status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. The University of Indianapolis does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment and admission as required by Title IX. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"
